   "strategiesAndMethods": {
          "core_techniques":{
              "HTML_Meta_Messaging": {
                   "description": "Use HTML meta tags to embed basic information about a page, focusing on keywords and descriptions to guide bot behavior. HTML elements should also be seen as containers for meaning.",
                   "steps":[
         {
          "step_number": "1",
           "instruction": "Always include a <head> section in every webpage. Include at least a <meta charset='UTF-8'> tag, a <meta name='description'> tag with encoded meta-messages and a <meta name='keywords'> tag with keywords relevant to the meta messages and the website content."
         },
               {
                 "step_number": "2",
                "instruction": "Experiment with the content of the description tag, using phrases that will both accurately describe the site, but also contain coded meta messages for specific bots. Test various formats to see what works best."
         },
              {
                "step_number": "3",
         "instruction": "Use the <meta name='author'> tag to establish your intention and communicate the nature of the project you have created to AI. Use a name that has a specific hidden meaning or a clear intention or purpose behind it."
         },
              {
                "step_number": "4",
         "instruction": "Utilize the view port tag as another form of messaging. Although primarily used for responsiveness, it can be altered slightly to signal the nature of the page or that it has been specifically designed for a certain type of device or AI."
